{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115772",
      "title": "Making Sense of Signal Effects",
      "lectureOrder": 138,
      "videoOrder": 131,
      "sourceHash": "8b8bc20ccb02b2b46e024779cc73020e66695599247dac8ccc85d92d813bb025",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.42,
          "end": 3.42,
          "en": "So you did now learn about more lifecycle hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.42,
          "end": 6.36,
          "en": "and about ViewChild and ContentChild.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.36,
          "end": 9.57,
          "en": "Before we continue working on that new ticket component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.57,
          "end": 12.72,
          "en": "and we make sure that we actually use the submitted values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.72,
          "end": 15.51,
          "en": "to advance our application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.51,
          "end": 20.22,
          "en": "there's one last kind of lifecycle related feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.22,
          "end": 22.74,
          "en": "I also want to introduce you to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.74,
          "end": 25.29,
          "en": "though it's not technically a lifecycle hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.29,
          "end": 27.513,
          "en": "instead it's a Signal feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.41,
          "end": 29.4,
          "en": "And to understand it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.4,
          "end": 32.193,
          "en": "I'll go to the server status component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.33,
          "end": 35.37,
          "en": "In there in my application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.37,
          "end": 39.66,
          "en": "I'm currently not using a Signal, but I'll change that now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.66,
          "end": 42.63,
          "en": "I'll change the current status property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.63,
          "end": 46.45,
          "en": "from being a regular property to being a Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.37,
          "end": 51.963,
          "en": "by executing the Signal function provided by Angular core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.01,
          "end": 57.21,
          "en": "So I want to manage my state here with help of signals now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.21,
          "end": 59.82,
          "en": "For that, I'll initialize this Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.82,
          "end": 62.13,
          "en": "to the value offline",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.13,
          "end": 64.86,
          "en": "and therefore current status now will hold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.86,
          "end": 66.87,
          "en": "a Signal as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.87,
          "end": 70.28999999999999,
          "en": "And hence the type of current status is no longer one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.28999999999999,
          "end": 75.28999999999999,
          "en": "of these strings, but instead it's a writeable Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.78,
          "end": 78.39,
          "en": "But I'll take advantage of the fact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.39,
          "end": 81.6,
          "en": "that I can overwrite the inferred type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.6,
          "end": 84.84,
          "en": "of the value wrapped by that Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.84,
          "end": 87.06,
          "en": "by adding angle brackets here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.06,
          "end": 90.53999999999999,
          "en": "And I'll tell TypeScript that the value managed by",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.53999999999999,
          "end": 93.63,
          "en": "that Signal is not any kind of string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.63,
          "end": 95.913,
          "en": "which would be its inferred value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.96000000000001,
          "end": 100.35,
          "en": "but instead that it's one of these three strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.35,
          "end": 104.43299999999999,
          "en": "Initially it's offline, but it could be online or unknown.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.77000000000001,
          "end": 109.83,
          "en": "So now current status is a Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.83,
          "end": 112.28999999999999,
          "en": "Therefore if you want to update it, we have to do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.28999999999999,
          "end": 114.84,
          "en": "with help of the set method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.84,
          "end": 118.8,
          "en": "So in all those places where I change the Signal value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.8,
          "end": 121.173,
          "en": "that's now done with set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.15,
          "end": 128.07,
          "en": "And in the template we now have to read that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.07,
          "end": 132.303,
          "en": "So we have to execute current status as a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 133.65,
          "end": 134.483,
          "en": "Like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.46,
          "end": 138.75,
          "en": "With that if we save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 138.75,
          "end": 142.95,
          "en": "all this application still works the way it did before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 142.95,
          "end": 146.493,
          "en": "but now I'm using a Signal in the server status component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 147.81,
          "end": 150.75,
          "en": "Now why am I doing that though?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 150.75,
          "end": 153.39,
          "en": "Well, because sometimes you have code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.39,
          "end": 157.653,
          "en": "that should be executed whenever a Signal value changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 159,
          "end": 162.36,
          "en": "Now, if you're using a Signal in a template like I'm doing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 162.36,
          "end": 164.67000000000002,
          "en": "it here in multiple places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 164.67000000000002,
          "end": 166.89,
          "en": "Angular will automatically set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 166.89,
          "end": 169.68,
          "en": "and manage a subscription for you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.68,
          "end": 171.75,
          "en": "and it'll automatically update the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 171.75,
          "end": 173.973,
          "en": "whenever the Signal value changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 175.02,
          "end": 176.43,
          "en": "But what if you wanna listen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 176.43,
          "end": 180.18,
          "en": "to a change in your TypeScript component class?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 180.18,
          "end": 182.7,
          "en": "There let's say in the constructor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 182.7,
          "end": 187.47,
          "en": "if I read this Signal value like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 187.47,
          "end": 190.473,
          "en": "Angular will not set up a subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 191.67,
          "end": 195.72,
          "en": "Instead, if I read it like this and I reload here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 195.72,
          "end": 200.72,
          "en": "you will see that offline gets logged here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 201.03,
          "end": 203.34,
          "en": "That's coming from that server status component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 203.34,
          "end": 206.25,
          "en": "TypeScript file from the constructor there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 206.25,
          "end": 210.32999999999998,
          "en": "But then we never see any other offline, online",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 210.32999999999998,
          "end": 212.973,
          "en": "or unknown log thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 213.87,
          "end": 215.91,
          "en": "We only have this one log.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 215.91,
          "end": 218.73,
          "en": "And the reason for that is that, as I just explained,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 218.73,
          "end": 223.56,
          "en": "Angular does not set up a subscription here, which is good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 223.56,
          "end": 227.4,
          "en": "That means you can safely read Signal values in your",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 227.4,
          "end": 231.483,
          "en": "TypeScript code without setting up accidental subscriptions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 232.32,
          "end": 235.05,
          "en": "But the downside is that sometimes you might want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 235.05,
          "end": 238.65,
          "en": "to set up a subscription and you're not getting it then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 238.65,
          "end": 242.82,
          "en": "that's why Angular offers you a special function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 242.82,
          "end": 245.49,
          "en": "The effect function, which is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 245.49,
          "end": 247.983,
          "en": "of course imported from Angular core,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 249.63,
          "end": 253.713,
          "en": "which you can execute in your constructor for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 255.84,
          "end": 258.93,
          "en": "And effect takes a function as an argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 258.93,
          "end": 262.77,
          "en": "And if you then use a Signal in that function that's passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 262.77,
          "end": 267.093,
          "en": "to effect, Angular will set up a subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 268.44,
          "end": 271.89,
          "en": "So by moving this code into this function that's passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 271.89,
          "end": 276.513,
          "en": "to effect, Angular now does set up a subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 278.04,
          "end": 280.68,
          "en": "And it it'll automatically clean up that subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 280.68,
          "end": 283.983,
          "en": "if that component should ever get removed from the dorm.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 285,
          "end": 287.19,
          "en": "But with that, if I now save that and I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 287.19,
          "end": 290.38,
          "en": "you'll see that now I got offline here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 291.69,
          "end": 295.32,
          "en": "and we'll get new logs from time to time like here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 295.32,
          "end": 299.673,
          "en": "with online whenever this Signal value changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 301.38,
          "end": 304.02,
          "en": "And that can be a useful feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 304.02,
          "end": 306.93,
          "en": "And therefore, whilst effect is not technically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 306.93,
          "end": 308.13,
          "en": "a lifecycle hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 308.13,
          "end": 310.86,
          "en": "it's a very important function you should at least",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 310.86,
          "end": 313.44,
          "en": "know about because it does allow you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 313.44,
          "end": 318.06,
          "en": "to run code when Signal values change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 318.06,
          "end": 320.4,
          "en": "which you might not need all the time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 320.4,
          "end": 322.38,
          "en": "but which you might need sometimes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 322.38,
          "end": 326.373,
          "en": "And that's therefore how you can use that effect function.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
